-- title:
--   Normalised K₁(mathfrak pᵥ^ℓ)-newvector from a trivial-Euler functional equation
-- statement:
--   Fix a place $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, write $\mathbb Q_v$ for `v.adicCompletion ℚ`, $N(v)$ for `Ideal.absNorm v.asIdeal`, and $\psi_v$ for the standard local additive character [`NumberField.StandardAddChar.psiLocal ℚ v`](def/LanglandsTunnell_StandardLocalConstantsAt.html#L65); let $\ell$ be a natural number with $1\le\ell$.
--
--   The data are: a function $W_0$ on $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$ which is a local Whittaker datum for $\psi_v^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLocalWhittakerDatum`, that is, $W_0(u(x,y,z)g)=\psi_v^{-1}(x+y)W_0(g)$ for all upper unipotent $u(x,y,z)$ and all $g$, $W_0(1)=1$, the Whittaker-uniqueness property `HasWhittakerMultOne` for the cyclic representation generated by $W_0$, the property that $W_0$ lies in the cyclic span `gl3CyclicSubspace F` of every non-zero $F$ in its own cyclic span, the existence of an open subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$ fixing $W_0$ under right translation, and, for each open subgroup $U_v$, a finite set $B$ of functions whose $\mathbb C$-span contains every $U_v$-right-invariant element of `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀`; a central invariance hypothesis `hZ` stating that $W_0(g\cdot d\,I_3)=W_0(g)$ for every $g$ and every unit $d$ of $\mathbb Q_v$ with $|d|=1$ and $|d-1|\le \exp(-\ell)$; a non-zero complex number $\varepsilon$; and two polynomials $E,E_d\in\mathbb C[X]$ subject to $E=1$ and $E_d=1$, so that every Euler factor occurring below is $1$ while the polynomials remain present formally.
--
--   The single remaining hypothesis `hdat` is a package of Rankin–Selberg statements for $\mathrm{GL}_3\times\mathrm{GL}_2$ at $v$. It applies to every $\varpi$ in the valuation ring whose image $\pi$ in $\mathbb Q_v$ is non-zero and satisfies $|\pi|=\exp(-1)$, every pair $a_1,a_2\in\mathbb C$ with $a_1a_2\neq0$, and every pair of functions $W_2,W_2^{\vee}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ subject to the clauses: $W_2(n(x)g)=\psi_v(x)W_2(g)$ and $W_2^{\vee}(n(x)g)=\psi_v^{-1}(x)W_2^{\vee}(g)$ for the standard unipotent $n(x)$; right invariance of $W_2$ and of $W_2^{\vee}$ under [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v ⊤`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178), the pullback along the local embedding of the finite-adelic level-one subgroup for the unit ideal; the normalisations $W_2(1)=W_2^{\vee}(1)=1$; the central values $W_2(g\cdot \pi I_2)=\bigl(a_1a_2/N(v)\bigr)W_2(g)$ and $W_2^{\vee}(g\cdot \pi I_2)=\bigl(N(v)/(a_1a_2)\bigr)W_2^{\vee}(g)$; and the torus values $W_2(\mathrm{diag}(\pi^m,1))=\mathtt{torusFactor}\,N(v)\,(a_1+a_2)\,\bigl(a_1a_2/N(v)\bigr)\,m$ and $W_2^{\vee}(\mathrm{diag}(\pi^m,1))=\mathtt{torusFactor}\,N(v)\,\bigl(N(v)(a_1+a_2)/(a_1a_2)\bigr)\,\bigl(N(v)/(a_1a_2)\bigr)\,m$ for all $m\in\mathbb Z$, where `torusFactor` is given by the Hecke recursion `heckeRecursionSeq` for $m\ge0$ and by $0$ for $m<0$. Giving $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ its Borel structure, `hdat` then asserts, for all Haar measures $\mu_2$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ and $\mu_N$ on the image of `unipotentGL2Hom`, and for every $W$ in `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀`, the existence of polynomials $p,q,p_d,q_d$ and reals $\sigma_2,\sigma_3$ with $q\neq0$, $q_d\neq0$ such that, with respect to $\mu_2$ weighted by the density [`HaarQuotient.density`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L25) of the unipotent subgroup (the measure representing integration over $N_2\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2$): for $\operatorname{Re}s>\sigma_2$ the function $g\mapsto W(\iota g)W_2(g)\,|\det g|^{s-1/2}$ is integrable, where $\iota$ is the embedding `iotaGL` of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ into $\mathrm{GL}_3$ in the upper-left block and $|\cdot|$ is the module `modulus`; for $\operatorname{Re}(1-s)>\sigma_3$ the function $g\mapsto \bigl(\mathtt{dualWhittakerFn3}\,W\bigr)\bigl(\iota g\cdot\iota((\pi I_2)^{-\ell})\bigr)W_2^{\vee}(g)\,|\det g|^{(1-s)-1/2}$ is integrable, where $\mathtt{dualWhittakerFn3}\,W(h)=W(w_3\,{}^{t}h^{-1})$ for the long Weyl element $w_3$; the local integral [`RSCarrier.rsLocalIntegral`](def/LanglandsTunnell_RSCarrier.html#L16) at $s$ formed from $W\circ\iota$, $W_2$ and $\delta(g)=|\det g|$ satisfies $\Psi(s)\,q(N(v)^{-s})=p(N(v)^{-s})$ for $\operatorname{Re}s>\sigma_2$; the corresponding dual integral at $1-s$, formed from the translated dual function and $W_2^{\vee}$, satisfies $\widetilde\Psi(1-s)\,q_d(N(v)^{-(1-s)})=p_d(N(v)^{-(1-s)})$ for $\operatorname{Re}(1-s)>\sigma_3$; and, for all $s\in\mathbb C$, the cleared functional equation
--   $$p_d(N(v)^{-(1-s)})\,q(N(v)^{-s})\,E_d\bigl(a_1^{-1}N(v)^{-(1/2-s)}\bigr)E_d\bigl(a_2^{-1}N(v)^{-(1/2-s)}\bigr)=p(N(v)^{-s})\,q_d(N(v)^{-(1-s)})\,E\bigl(a_1N(v)^{-(s+1/2)}\bigr)E\bigl(a_2N(v)^{-(s+1/2)}\bigr)\varepsilon^{2}.$$
--
--   Conclusion: there exists $W$ in `gl3CyclicSubspace W₀` with the following three properties.
--
--   First, $W(gk)=W(g)$ for all $g\in\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_v)$ and all $k$ in the set `congruenceK1 (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v ℓ`, that is all $k$ such that $k$ and $k^{-1}$ have all entries of valuation at most $1$ and $|k_{2,0}|\le\exp(-\ell)$, $|k_{2,1}|\le\exp(-\ell)$, $|k_{2,2}-1|\le\exp(-\ell)$.
--
--   Second, $W(1)=1$.
--
--   Third, for every $\varpi$ whose image $\pi$ is non-zero with $|\pi|=\exp(-1)$, every $a_1,a_2$ with $a_1a_2\neq0$, every function $W_2$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ satisfying the five clauses listed above for $W_2$ (the $\psi_v$-equivariance under unipotents, right invariance under [`AdelicDock.localLevelOne (𝓞 ℚ) ℚ v ⊤`](def/AdelicDock_LocalEmbedding.html#L178), $W_2(1)=1$, the central value $a_1a_2/N(v)$ and the `torusFactor` values with parameters $N(v)$, $a_1+a_2$, $a_1a_2/N(v)$), and all Haar measures $\mu_2$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ and $\mu_N$ on the image of `unipotentGL2Hom`, there is a real $\sigma_2$ such that for all $s$ with $\operatorname{Re}s>\sigma_2$ the function $g\mapsto W(\iota g)W_2(g)\,|\det g|^{s-1/2}$ is integrable against $\mu_2$ weighted by [`HaarQuotient.density`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L25), and
--   $$\Psi(s)\,E\bigl(a_1N(v)^{-(s+1/2)}\bigr)\,E\bigl(a_2N(v)^{-(s+1/2)}\bigr)=\operatorname{vol}\bigl(\{g:\ g=nk,\ n\in\operatorname{range}(\mathtt{unipotentGL2Hom}),\ k\in \mathtt{localLevelOne}\ (\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q})\,\mathbb Q\,v\ \top\}\bigr),$$
--   where $\Psi(s)$ is [`RSCarrier.rsLocalIntegral`](def/LanglandsTunnell_RSCarrier.html#L16) at $s$ for $W\circ\iota$, $W_2$ and $\delta(g)=|\det g|$, and the right-hand side is the real number obtained from the measure of that set under the same weighted measure, viewed in $\mathbb C$. No dual integral and no dual function occur in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the abstract form, with all Euler polynomials set equal to $1$, of the newvector step in the Rankin–Selberg analysis of a $\mathrm{GL}_3$ Whittaker datum at a finite place: from a $\mathrm{GL}_3\times\mathrm{GL}_2$ functional equation valid against all spherical $\mathrm{GL}_2$ Whittaker functions and their contragredients, a vector in the cyclic span is produced which is $K_1(\mathfrak p_v^{\ell})$-invariant, normalised at $1$, and whose local integral against spherical data equals the volume of the cell $N_2K_v$. It feeds `exists_mem_gl3CyclicSubspace_congruenceK1_invariant_iotaGL_eq_bump_of_localZeta31_fe_one` in the converse-theorem part of the Langlands–Tunnell argument.
